#DESCRIPTION
Hybrid PIC (kinetic ions / fluid electrons) performance benchmark.  A Hall-term
whistler wave (the standard hybrid workload) on a 1D periodic grid sized to be a
representative scaling benchmark: 128 X cells, 2000 macroparticles/cell, so the
particle mover and the explicit Ohm's-law + Faraday field advance both dominate
the wall-clock.  This is the hybrid counterpart of performance/PARAM.in (the
full-PIC beam benchmark) and is exercised by tests/validate_performance.py and
by the memory regression selection in tests/capture_memory.py.

The solver setup is the one validated by tests/whistler/PARAM.in.hybrid: the
same Hall-only Ohm's law, the same grid-mode hyper-resistivity, and the B
sub-cycling scaled to this (finer) grid, so the benchmark exercises the same
field-advance machinery as the hybrid validation test instead of a private
configuration.  See the RESISTIVITY / BSUBCYCLE notes below.

Normalization matches the hybrid test family (whistler): lNormSI ~ d_i,
uNormSI = speed of light (set to v_A so c/v_A = 1), so d_i ~ v_A ~ 1 and
(for the proton) B ~ Omega_i ~ 1 in code units.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
128                     nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

Standard Maxwell/GMRES solver disabled; use the Ohm's-law + Faraday hybrid
field advance instead.
#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

Hall-only: resistive and electron-pressure-gradient terms off (0.0).  This is
what isolates the Hall/whistler workload, exactly as in the whistler deck.
#RESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaResistivity  [m^2/s, SI magnetic diffusivity]

Grid-mode hyper-resistivity, the same setting as tests/whistler/PARAM.in.hybrid
(0.0 / grid / 1.0e-2): eta_h = 4*pi * C_h * dx^4 / dt, i.e. a damping
gamma_h = C_h * (k*dx)^4 / dt that acts only on the badly resolved harmonics.
At dx = 0.05 it is negligible where the physics lives (gamma_h = 1.2e-4 at
k d_i = 1 against omega = 1.6) and it only reaches the few-cell band that the
explicit Hall advance cannot integrate (gamma_h = 48 at k dx = pi, against the
~11 per-step growth measured below).  Damping of that band is NOT sufficient on
its own here: with C_h = 1e-2 the deck still diverges at nBSubcycle = 8, so the
sub-cycling below carries the stability at this resolution.
#HYPERRESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaHyperSI
grid                    etaHyperMode
1.0e-2                  etaHyperCh

#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
0.0                     electronTemperature  [eV]
1.0                     electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0

Sub-cycle the explicit Hall advance (limited by the grid-scale whistler mode):
omega_max * dt_sub < 2.785 (RK4).  32 sub-steps give the same margin as the
whistler deck's 8 at dx = 0.1: the grid-scale whistler frequency goes as dx^-2,
and 8 * (0.1/0.05)^2 = 32, so both run at omega_max * dt_sub ~ 2.5.  Measured
here: 8 sub-steps are over the limit and diverge in the FIRST step (max(uth)
0.093 -> 6569, CFL 2627, particles leaving the periodic box by ~1e4 cell lengths
per step), while 16 / 32 / 64 are all stable for the full TimeMax.  32 is used
so the benchmark carries the same stability margin as the validation deck, and
the margin is cheap: the whole TimeMax = 1.0 run takes 2.7 / 3.2 / 3.8 s at
16 / 32 / 64 sub-steps (the particle mover is a large share of that).
#BSUBCYCLE
32                      nBSubcycle

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]
1.0439e-8               bx [T]       uniform guide field Bx0 (B_code ~ 1)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TESTCASE
HybridWave

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
1.0e5                   uNormSI   [m/s] tNorm = 1 s; sets cLight_SI = uNormSI

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
100                     dnSavePic
100                     dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
2000                    nParticle per cell in X
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#COMOVING
F                       solvePartInCoMov
0                       nSmoothBackGroundU

#UPWINDE
F                       useUpwindE
0.0                     limiterThetaE

#UPWINDB
F                       doSmoothB
0.0                     theta

#SAVEPLOT
0                                 nPlot

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
1.0                     TimeMax

#RUN
